WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:04.920
Brainwashing, betrayal, bows, and&nbsp;
ballads. The story of "The Hunger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:09.400
Games" begins way before Katniss&nbsp;
— and even before Snow. Here's the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:14.400
whole timeline. Spoilers ahead for&nbsp;
the entire "Hunger Games" franchise.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:20.160
The nation of Panem doesn't just appear overnight&nbsp;
— it forms in the ruins of our civilization. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:25.360
world changes forever with the onset of climate&nbsp;
change. Natural disasters like fires, droughts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:29.520
and storms cause the planet's resources&nbsp;
to dwindle. Countries begin to fight over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:35.920
the remaining resources, causing war to break out&nbsp;
across the globe. With such widespread bloodshed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:41.160
governments around the world begin to collapse&nbsp;
and the human population rapidly decreases,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:43.880
nearly creating an extinction-level event.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:48.720
From the ashes of society in North America&nbsp;
rises Panem — a new nation with a capital&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:53.200
based in the Rocky Mountains. History's a&nbsp;
little murky around this period. It isn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:58.520
clear exactly when Panem forms after the&nbsp;
fall of other preexisting civilizations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.400
or when Panem divides into districts.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:04.160
"You're not off to a real good start."

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:09.160
What we do know is that each district&nbsp;
provides the Capitol with a vital resource,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:14.160
though the districts are reliant on the Capitol&nbsp;
to ensure the distribution of those resources.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:19.680
The Capitol exploits the districts it rules&nbsp;
over by controlling its exclusive access to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:25.040
necessities, and this eventually causes&nbsp;
the districts to turn on the Capitol.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:29.240
The idea for the Hunger Games comes long&nbsp;
before the rebellion that causes its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:34.400
implementation. Crassus Snow, future&nbsp;
President Coriolanus Snow's father,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:38.480
attends the Capitol's University with&nbsp;
his best friend Casca Highbottom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:43.520
the Dean of the Academy Coriolanus attends&nbsp;
years later. The two are in a class taught&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:49.040
by Dr. Volumnia Gaul, a scientist who&nbsp;
later becomes the first Head Gamesmaker.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:54.640
While Gaul and Crassus Snow get along well, Gaul&nbsp;
and Highbottom do not. For their final project,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:59.240
Gaul tasks the students with developing a&nbsp;
hypothetical punishment that would ensure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:03.440
their enemies never forgot what they did&nbsp;
to them. Snow works with Highbottom and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:07.000
gets him drunk while hearing what&nbsp;
he has to say about the assignment.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:12.520
Snow turns his idea in as their assignment. The&nbsp;
two fight over this; Highbottom never forgives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:18.200
Snow and eventually takes out that frustration on&nbsp;
Snow's son. Even though it's originally meant as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:23.720
a class assignment, Gaul uses the proposal to&nbsp;
create an annual punishment for the districts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:29.360
after the rebellion, and Highbottom goes down&nbsp;
in history as the brains behind the games.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:34.360
At an unknown point after the founding of&nbsp;
Panem, the districts begin to grow restless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:39.480
with the power dynamics at play. This part of&nbsp;
history is documented mostly by the Capitol,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:44.080
and since they're pretty good at propaganda,&nbsp;
it's hard to say how much is true. Capitol&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:48.880
children learn that "rebels" in District&nbsp;
13 were the instigators behind the First&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:54.240
Rebellion and used its privilege as a&nbsp;
nuclear research facility to its advantage.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:57.360
"This was the uprising that rocked our land."

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.760
War spreads throughout Panem with&nbsp;
other districts rising up and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:03.400
holding their resources hostage from the Capitol.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:07.240
The unrest continues to grow over&nbsp;
the course of around three years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:12.760
turning into air raids on the country's political&nbsp;
center. The ruling class of Panem spends most of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:18.000
the war under the grip of the districts. Because&nbsp;
of its reliance on them for goods and services,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:24.400
the elite often find themselves without power or&nbsp;
essentials as different districts join the cause.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:28.920
When the districts invade the Capitol, the&nbsp;
direction of the war turns. Despite being the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:34.720
alleged starting point of the rebellion, District&nbsp;
13 begins to pull back and eventually brokers a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:40.160
deal with the Capitol. The conflict ends with the&nbsp;
secret agreement that District 13 will be allowed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:46.240
to live on ... just not as a member of Panem. The&nbsp;
other 12 districts watch as the Capitol bombs and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:51.320
destroys the surface of District 13, which&nbsp;
leads them to believe the district is gone.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:55.240
Without 13's support, the rest of the&nbsp;
districts can no longer maintain their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:59.480
war efforts, falling to the Capitol as&nbsp;
the military sweeps through the country.

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:05.000
As the Capitol regains control, they develop&nbsp;
the Treaty of Treason. The treaty creates a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:07.880
variety of restrictions for the citizens of Panem,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:11.480
including banning communication&nbsp;
and travel between districts.

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:15.400
It also leads to the implementation of&nbsp;
their punishment. The Hunger Games is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:19.960
the most significant part of the treaty —&nbsp;
the annual event that forces the districts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:24.901
to sacrifice two children every year&nbsp;
in a televised battle to the death.

00:04:24.901 --> 00:04:29.920
"Since the Dark Days, our great&nbsp;
nation has known only peace."

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:33.560
The First Rebellion and Dark&nbsp;
Days also mark a turning point&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:37.920
in Coriolanus Snow's life. Just&nbsp;
5 years old when the war begins,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:43.040
the young Snow watches on as the civilization&nbsp;
he grows up with almost falls to the districts.

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:47.000
Snow's mother dies in childbirth,&nbsp;
and shortly after, his father,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:51.200
who has risen through the military&nbsp;
ranks, dies in rebel fire. With his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:55.600
cousin Tigris' parents also dead, the&nbsp;
two of them live with their grandmother.

00:04:55.600 --> 00:05:01.280
The Snow name affords the future president of&nbsp;
Panem many privileges early on, but that all goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:07.120
away with District 13. Most of the family's assets&nbsp;
are in nuclear research, so when District 13 is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:13.040
"bombed" the family's riches and status plummet.&nbsp;
Even as Snow becomes an adult, his home is still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:18.400
significantly damaged from the First Rebellion&nbsp;
because his family can't afford the repairs.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:21.880
The first nine Hunger Games are&nbsp;
drastically different from what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:25.920
the event eventually becomes by, oh, the 74th one.

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:30.880
When it is time for The Games to begin,&nbsp;
all 24 tributes enter the Capitol Arena&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:35.880
with few weapons and no food and are left to&nbsp;
fight to the death. Once crowned the winner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:40.160
the victor goes home, returning to their life&nbsp;
as it was before they competed in The Hunger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:46.360
Games. The early Games were particularly barbaric,&nbsp;
even compared to later evolutions of the event.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:47.760
"This is the price of peace."

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:52.680
The only thing that remains unchanged from&nbsp;
the early games is the selection of tributes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:57.040
From the beginning, the tributes from each&nbsp;
district are chosen through a lottery system,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:02.160
selecting one female and one male&nbsp;
child between the ages of 12 and 18.

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:07.880
The 10th Hunger Games is when the event changes&nbsp;
to create a more watchable experience. To do this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:12.280
several key elements that later become&nbsp;
staples in The Games are introduced,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:17.200
including mentors, the ability to give gifts&nbsp;
to tributes once they are in the arena,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:21.640
and tribute interviews. The first mentors&nbsp;
are Academy students who are just Capitol&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:26.600
teens trying to finish their high school-level&nbsp;
education before heading off to University.

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:31.440
To help introduce these new elements, several&nbsp;
changes take place in how The Games function.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:35.520
Rather than The Games starting soon after&nbsp;
all of the tributes arrive in the Capitol,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:40.240
the contestants are instead placed in an&nbsp;
old animal enclosure in the Capitol Zoo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:45.200
essentially on display for Capitol citizens&nbsp;
to come and see. Over several days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:50.520
they tour the arena, meet with their mentors, and&nbsp;
participate in interviews on Capitol television.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:55.800
Starting with the 10th Games, the event&nbsp;
moves in a more spectacle-like direction.

00:06:55.800 --> 00:07:00.240
"Your role is to turn these children&nbsp;
into spectacles, not survivors."

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:06.280
Coriolanus Snow is one of the first mentors,&nbsp;
overseeing and advising Lucy Gray Baird,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:11.720
the musically gifted female tribute from District&nbsp;
12 during the 10th Hunger Games. This begins his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.720 --> 00:07:17.120
close connection with The Hunger Games, moving&nbsp;
from mentor to a Gamesmaker apprentice while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:22.440
attending University. The young Snow connects&nbsp;
with his tribute, Lucy Gray and uses tricks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:27.400
to ensure she becomes the victor, making him&nbsp;
the first mentor to coach a winning tribute.

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:31.920
While working as a mentor, he writes the&nbsp;
proposal for the implementation of a betting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:36.840
and odds system and the ability to send food&nbsp;
to tributes in the arena — two ways Capitol&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:42.640
citizens can "participate" and create an emotional&nbsp;
attachment to The Games. He also gets to see and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:48.120
learn about one of the muttations — Dr. Gaul's&nbsp;
snakes — before she drops them in the arena.

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:54.320
After Highbottom discovers that Snow used that&nbsp;
info to cheat to help Lucy Gray win, Snow becomes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.320 --> 00:08:00.280
a Peacekeeper. But before long, he heads back to&nbsp;
the Capitol and starts an apprenticeship under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:07.040
Dr. Gaul to be a Gamesmaker. During this time, he&nbsp;
continues introducing new concepts for the Games.

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:10.760
After winning the 10th Hunger Games and&nbsp;
returning to her life in District 12,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:13.760
Lucy Gray Baird continues to play music.

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:19.040
The atmosphere in District 12 is less than ideal,&nbsp;
to put it lightly. People are really struggling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:24.760
with the newly reinforced regime of the Capitol,&nbsp;
and as Lucy Gray watches these events play out in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.760 --> 00:08:29.920
her home, she takes to her guitar to express her&nbsp;
thoughts on the subject. She writes "The Hanging&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:35.520
Tree" about the death of Arlo Chance, a miner&nbsp;
and supporter of the rebellion. It is one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:41.160
many songs she writes, but this one has the most&nbsp;
impact after her disappearance and presumed death.

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:46.640
Despite the banning of music, the song survives&nbsp;
for generations, with Katniss' father teaching it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:52.120
to her before his death. While considered an act&nbsp;
of rebellion by Peacekeepers when it is written,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:56.000
the song becomes synonymous with the&nbsp;
Second Rebellion when Katniss sings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.000 --> 00:09:02.200
it during a rebellion-filmed TV spot in&nbsp;
"The Hunger Games: Mockingjay – Part 1."

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:04.840
"A little on the nose, but of course, so is war."

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:10.040
When it comes time to select tributes for the&nbsp;
74th annual Hunger Games, everything proceeds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:16.320
as usual ... until Primrose Everdeen is drawn as&nbsp;
the female tribute for District 12. Prim is only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:21.240
12 years old, meaning this is her first year&nbsp;
of eligibility for the Games, and has already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:26.720
had to endure the loss of her father in a mining&nbsp;
accident years prior. Unwilling to allow Prim to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:32.240
be selected for almost certain death, her older&nbsp;
sister, Katniss Everdeen volunteers to compete&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:38.240
in her place. Peeta, the son of a local baker,&nbsp;
is chosen as the male tribute from District 12.

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:42.760
Although both Katniss and Peeta know only&nbsp;
one of them will make it out of the arena,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:47.040
they grow fond of one another in the days&nbsp;
leading up to the Games. During their training,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:52.160
Katniss establishes herself as an accomplished&nbsp;
archer, while Peeta impresses his fellow tributes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:57.120
with his natural strength and his uncanny&nbsp;
ability to paint tree bark. Meanwhile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.120 --> 00:10:02.000
back in District 12, Katniss' best friend&nbsp;
Gale Hawthorne looks after Katniss' mother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:07.720
and sister as they all watch the TV coverage.&nbsp;
All these people may seem like normal citizens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.720 --> 00:10:11.520
but they turn out to be pretty&nbsp;
important in the years to come.

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:16.160
As the 74th Hunger Games begin, Katniss&nbsp;
ventures out on her own. She becomes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:19.360
convinced that Peeta is working&nbsp;
with other tributes to kill her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:23.840
even though he's actually trying to protect&nbsp;
her by throwing them off her scent. Eventually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:29.560
Katniss teams up with Rue, the 12-year-old tribute&nbsp;
from District 11, and things start looking up.

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:34.440
"We're gonna be okay."

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:39.240
Unfortunately, they aren't okay. Rue&nbsp;
is killed, and Katniss mourns her by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:43.560
covering her body with flowers — an&nbsp;
action that galvanizes District 11.

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:49.280
Following Rue's death, a change to the rules is&nbsp;
announced: Two victors may be crowned this year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:53.920
provided they're from the same district. Peeta&nbsp;
and Katniss promptly team up to defeat the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:59.520
other tributes. This strategy wins the hearts of&nbsp;
Capitol sponsors, who enjoy what they perceive as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:04.560
a blooming romance between the two. Thanks to&nbsp;
the timely supplies they send, some very quick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:09.560
thinking, and a fair amount of luck, Katniss and&nbsp;
Peeta become the final two tributes standing.

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:14.520
But then the announcer reveals that the&nbsp;
previous rule change has been undone:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:17.800
Only one of them will be allowed&nbsp;
to leave the arena alive. Neither&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.800 --> 00:11:21.880
Katniss nor Peeta is willing to kill the&nbsp;
other, so they resolve to kill themselves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:26.440
by eating poisonous berries. Panicked at&nbsp;
the thought of not having a victor at all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:31.600
the announcer changes the rules yet again to&nbsp;
allow for two victors, ending the Games. Head&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:38.440
Gamemaker Seneca Crane is subsequently executed&nbsp;
by President Coriolanus Snow for this decision.

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:43.800
"The Hunger Games: Catching Fire" opens as&nbsp;
the citizens of Panem prepare for the 75th&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:49.240
Hunger Games. In the lead-up to each Games, it's&nbsp;
customary for the winner of the prior bloodbath&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.240 --> 00:11:54.920
to go on a "Victory Tour" of the 12 districts&nbsp;
to drum up enthusiasm, as well as demonstrate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.920 --> 00:12:00.560
loyalty to the Capitol. But Katniss and Peeta's&nbsp;
defiance in the 74th Hunger Games has stirred&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.560 --> 00:12:07.000
unrest ahead of the 75th Games. The people of&nbsp;
Panem see Katniss as a symbol of resistance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:11.480
and the Capitol isn't pleased. Before&nbsp;
Katniss and Peeta leave on their tour,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:16.760
President Snow tells Katniss she needs to convince&nbsp;
the public that her attempt to subvert the rules&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.760 --> 00:12:22.520
by eating the berries was motivated solely by&nbsp;
love for Peeta, or he will kill her family.

00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:26.678
"It must be a fragile system if it can&nbsp;
be brought down by just a few berries."&nbsp;

00:12:26.678 --> 00:12:31.520
"It is indeed. But not in the way you imagine."

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:35.680
Katniss and Peeta do their best to present&nbsp;
themselves as a legitimate couple during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:39.640
their tour. But it's not enough to&nbsp;
quench the anger of the districts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:44.880
which is spreading like wildfire. It doesn't help&nbsp;
that Katniss isn't a very convincing actress,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:49.600
and also prone to acting impulsively:&nbsp;
She intervenes in several instances of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:54.080
Capitol-sanctioned brutality. This only&nbsp;
strengthens the public's perception of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:58.560
her as the "Mockingjay," a potent&nbsp;
symbol of freedom and rebellion.

00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:03.080
The 75th Hunger Games are much different&nbsp;
than the ritual the year before. They're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:07.920
the third Quarter Quell — a special game&nbsp;
that takes place every 25 years. Still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:12.640
seeking to smother the people's anger,&nbsp;
Snow — along with newly appointed Head&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:17.440
Gamemaker Plutarch Heavensbee — decides&nbsp;
that the tributes will be selected from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:23.000
the existing pool of victors. Since Katniss is&nbsp;
the only living female victor from District 12,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:27.080
there is no question that she will be&nbsp;
among those forced to return to the arena.

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:30.760
Of District 12's two male&nbsp;
victors, Haymitch Abernathy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:34.320
victor of the 50th Games and&nbsp;
Katniss and Peeta's mentor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:39.880
is selected to compete. To Katniss'&nbsp;
horror, Peeta volunteers to take his place.

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:45.400
Once they've arrived at the Capitol, the mood of&nbsp;
the 75th Hunger Games' tributes is revealed to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:51.680
markedly different than that of previous years.&nbsp;
Already having survived one round of brutality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:55.920
this group is rightfully angry that instead&nbsp;
of being allowed to live out their lives in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:55.920 --> 00:14:00.600
peace and comfort, they are instead being&nbsp;
sent back into the arena. As they're older&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:05.000
and considerably more experienced than the&nbsp;
children typically selected for the Games,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:09.200
these tributes boldly try a number of&nbsp;
tactics to get the Games shut down.

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:15.720
Unbeknownst to Katniss, secret resistance&nbsp;
ally Plutarch Heavensbee meets with Haymitch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:21.000
as well as a number of other tributes, to conspire&nbsp;
about what will happen if the Games proceed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:26.680
Under instructions from president Alma Coin,&nbsp;
leader of District 13 — which not only exists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:32.280
but is actively plotting a rebellion — Heavensbee,&nbsp;
Haymitch, and several tributes including Finnick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.280 --> 00:14:38.160
and Johanna devise a plan to extract Katniss&nbsp;
and Peeta from the Games once they are underway.

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:43.040
The 75th Hunger Games' circular arena has&nbsp;
a large lake in the center and is divided&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:48.000
into 12 wedges. This time, Katniss and Peeta&nbsp;
immediately team up, and are quickly joined&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:54.160
by Finnick and elderly Mags. Although Mags&nbsp;
soon sacrifices herself to save the others,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:59.320
the rest survive and are joined by Johanna,&nbsp;
along with Wiress and Beetee from District 3.

00:14:59.320 --> 00:15:04.160
An accomplished engineer, Beetee devises&nbsp;
a plan to use one of the arena's precisely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:08.880
timed traps to their advantage. Using&nbsp;
a spool of copper wire, he intends to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:14.000
harness the electricity from a lightning&nbsp;
strike to electrocute the other tributes.

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:18.000
"How do we know the wire's not going to burn up?"
"Because I invented it."

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:22.240
Presumably, his intent following the&nbsp;
elimination of the other tributes is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:28.280
to trigger District 13's rescue plan — though of&nbsp;
course, Katniss and Peeta know nothing about this.

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:32.800
When the plan goes awry at the last second,&nbsp;
Katniss wraps the end of the copper wire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:38.560
around an arrow and shoots it at the force field&nbsp;
ceiling of the arena, right as lightning strikes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:43.960
The current is drawn into the dome, causing it to&nbsp;
short out and subsequently crumble. This allows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:50.560
a large District 13 ship to enter and extract&nbsp;
Katniss and several other tributes. Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:50.560 --> 00:15:56.840
Peeta and Johanna are left behind and sent to the&nbsp;
Capitol, while Katniss is taken to District 13.

00:15:56.840 --> 00:16:02.120
Unable to be rescued by District 13, Peeta and&nbsp;
Johanna are interrogated and tortured by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:07.000
Capitol. Peeta doesn't know anything about&nbsp;
the resistance, but Snow rightly assumes he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:12.400
can use him as leverage to influence Katniss.&nbsp;
Through a number of televised propaganda spots&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:17.640
filmed in the Capitol, Katniss sees Peeta&nbsp;
become ever more alarmingly brainwashed.

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:23.000
During this time, another former winner,&nbsp;
Annie Cresta, and Johanna are also tortured&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:27.400
by the Capitol, although they are not shown&nbsp;
on television as Peeta is. But the Capitol's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:32.560
actions are even worse than they think: When he&nbsp;
isn't filming propaganda spots, Peeta is being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:32.560 --> 00:16:38.120
subjected to vicious brainwashing techniques&nbsp;
which cause him to become fearful of Katniss.

00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:43.120
Although she would like nothing more than to&nbsp;
go charging into the Capitol to rescue Peeta,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:46.760
Katniss is now subject to the&nbsp;
administration of President Coin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:46.760 --> 00:16:52.240
who is determined to work more strategically. As&nbsp;
"The Hunger Games: Mockingjay — Part 1" opens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:57.840
Coin convinces Katniss to embrace her persona as&nbsp;
the Mockingjay and film a series of propaganda&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:57.840 --> 00:17:03.360
videos to inspire the people of Panem. With&nbsp;
District 12 reduced to smoking rubble and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:10.480
Katniss' mother, Prim, and Gale now residing in&nbsp;
District 13, Katniss feels she has no choice.

00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:16.720
"People of Panem, we fight. We dare&nbsp;
to end this hunger for justice."

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:20.960
Unfortunately for Coin, Katniss is no&nbsp;
more convincing when delivering scripted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:20.960 --> 00:17:25.600
monologues for a cause she believes&nbsp;
in than one she doesn't. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:30.920
she is occasionally inspired to improvise, and&nbsp;
manages to give a few impassioned speeches that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:30.920 --> 00:17:35.880
successfully rally the districts. Once again,&nbsp;
Snow doesn't like what Katniss is up to,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:41.120
and he finally orders an airborne attack on&nbsp;
District 13. Peeta is able to regain control of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:46.520
himself just long enough to warn Katniss and the&nbsp;
other residents of the district to take shelter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:46.520 --> 00:17:51.240
resulting in far fewer casualties&nbsp;
than there otherwise would have been.

00:17:51.240 --> 00:17:55.880
Finally, President Coin authorizes a&nbsp;
mission to rescue Peeta and the other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:55.880 --> 00:18:00.400
victors from the Capitol, though Katniss is&nbsp;
not allowed to join the rescue team. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:00.400 --> 00:18:05.560
she is tasked with filming a live broadcast&nbsp;
to Snow in the hopes of distracting him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:10.560
from seeing what's happening right under his&nbsp;
nose…until he reveals that he knows exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:16.080
what's happening. Yet somehow, Peeta, Johanna,&nbsp;
and Annie are successfully rescued. Gale, who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:21.760
participated in the rescue mission, observes that&nbsp;
finding and retrieving them was almost too easy.

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:27.960
"Every gun was back online and on us and&nbsp;
we flew right past them. They let us go."

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:32.880
The reason for this is made clear when&nbsp;
Katniss eagerly rushes to reunite with Peeta,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:37.600
only to have him viciously attack her. At this&nbsp;
point, it becomes clear to the resistance that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:37.600 --> 00:18:42.200
Snow has brainwashed Peeta into wanting&nbsp;
to kill Katniss, then allowed him to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:47.520
rescued. While the resistance's doctors work&nbsp;
diligently to counteract Peeta's brainwashing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:51.840
Katniss is told she will have to keep&nbsp;
her distance for the safety of them both.

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:56.120
As "The Hunger Games: Mockingjay — Part&nbsp;
2" begins, Katniss is determined to seek&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:56.120 --> 00:19:01.080
revenge for Peeta's condition. Following a&nbsp;
series of successful attacks by rebel forces,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:05.840
the Capitol troops withdraw from the districts&nbsp;
to regroup within the Capitol itself. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:05.840 --> 00:19:09.880
place a number of lethal traps called&nbsp;
"pods" around the outskirts of the city,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:09.880 --> 00:19:12.360
to prevent resistance fighters from advancing.

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:16.040
Fortunately, the resistance is able to&nbsp;
procure a device which allows them to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:16.040 --> 00:19:21.160
see the placement of most — but not all —&nbsp;
of these pods, increasing their chances of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:21.160 --> 00:19:26.000
being able to successfully reach the Capitol's&nbsp;
center, where President Snow resides. Katniss&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:30.520
and Gale are placed on a team dubbed the&nbsp;
"Star Squad," which is meant to follow the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:35.440
combat troops and film propaganda videos&nbsp;
showcasing the resistance's successes.

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:40.600
They've barely made it into the city when Peeta is&nbsp;
added to the group under Coin's orders, allegedly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:40.600 --> 00:19:45.800
to show the Capitol that he is still loyal to the&nbsp;
resistance. However, the team suspects he's there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:45.800 --> 00:19:51.520
to kill Katniss, since her high-profile status&nbsp;
as the Mockingjay poses a threat to Coin's power.

00:19:51.520 --> 00:19:55.960
"She doesn't like anybody or&nbsp;
anything that she can't control."&nbsp;

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:58.600
"So she would put my life in danger?"

00:19:58.600 --> 00:20:02.720
But despite their misgivings, the group&nbsp;
pushes deeper into the city. Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:05.320
between the pods and Peeta's violent programming,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:05.320 --> 00:20:10.480
this mission proves deadly for most of the&nbsp;
team, including Finnick. Only Katniss, Gale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:15.680
Peeta, and a couple members of the camera crew&nbsp;
make it to the center of the Capitol alive.

00:20:15.680 --> 00:20:20.120
Realizing that the Capitol is losing the war,&nbsp;
President Snow invites the remaining Capitol&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:24.200
citizens to gather around his mansion&nbsp;
and bring the children toward the gates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:27.680
in the hopes that a human shield will&nbsp;
dissuade the rebels from fighting their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:27.680 --> 00:20:33.240
way inside. But as Katniss and Gale work their&nbsp;
way toward the mansion disguised as civilians,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:38.240
fighting breaks out. They're separated when&nbsp;
Gale is arrested by Capitol Peacekeepers.

00:20:38.240 --> 00:20:43.480
Alone, Katniss nearly makes it to the gates of&nbsp;
President Snow's mansion. But as the Capitol's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:43.480 --> 00:20:48.040
citizens desperately pass their children&nbsp;
forward through the crowd, bombs are dropped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:53.560
from a Capitol airship, blasting Katniss off her&nbsp;
feet. When she opens her eyes, she sees all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:58.360
dead and wounded civilians, and the volunteer&nbsp;
medics who have rushed in to treat them. Just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:04.480
as Katniss spies Prim among the medics, a second&nbsp;
wave of bombs goes off, knocking Katniss out.

00:21:04.480 --> 00:21:09.360
Katniss awakens to the news that the rebels have&nbsp;
won the war, Snow has been taken into custody,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:14.200
and Prim is dead. After being given a room in&nbsp;
the mansion, Katniss goes to the greenhouse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:20.520
where Snow is being kept and demands an audience.&nbsp;
The condemned Snow reveals to her that it is Coin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:20.520 --> 00:21:24.920
not him, who's responsible for the&nbsp;
Capitol bombing and her sister's death.

00:21:24.920 --> 00:21:30.080
"I must concede, it was a&nbsp;
masterful move on Coin's part."

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:34.920
Horrified, Katniss realizes that Gale was&nbsp;
likely the one who gave Coin the idea,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:34.920 --> 00:21:37.160
driving a permanent wedge between them.

00:21:37.160 --> 00:21:41.800
Later, during a meeting with the leaders of the&nbsp;
resistance, several of the remaining victors are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:47.520
appalled when Coin suggests a new Hunger Games.&nbsp;
Capitol children will be the tributes this time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:47.520 --> 00:21:52.840
in order to satiate the people's need for&nbsp;
revenge without giving in to massive bloodshed.

00:21:52.840 --> 00:21:57.680
Katniss votes in favor of these new Games, on&nbsp;
the condition that she be the one to execute&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:57.680 --> 00:22:02.640
Snow. But when the time for this execution&nbsp;
comes, Katniss kills Coin instead. She has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:02.640 --> 00:22:07.520
realized that allowing Coin to remain in charge&nbsp;
will only lead to more of the same oppressive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:07.520 --> 00:22:13.640
conditions that got them into this situation. Snow&nbsp;
is subsequently killed by the angry spectators.

00:22:13.640 --> 00:22:18.320
Following the deaths of Presidents Coin&nbsp;
and Snow, Katniss is placed under arrest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:18.320 --> 00:22:23.560
but is then pardoned and allowed to return to&nbsp;
District 12. Commander Paylor of District 8 is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:23.560 --> 00:22:29.400
quickly elected Panem's new president. She acts&nbsp;
to abolish the Hunger Games, demolish the arenas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:29.400 --> 00:22:34.520
and build memorials to the many people who&nbsp;
died. It is implied that henceforth, Panem&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:34.520 --> 00:22:39.240
will be governed by its people, who will select&nbsp;
their leader through free and fair elections.

00:22:39.240 --> 00:22:44.000
Sometime during the years that follow, Katniss&nbsp;
marries Peeta and has two children with him. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:49.120
both still suffer from PTSD, with Peeta bearing&nbsp;
the worst of it due to the lingering effects of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:49.120 --> 00:22:54.680
his brainwashing — he sometimes has to ask for&nbsp;
Katniss' help in determining what is real. Though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:54.680 --> 00:22:59.440
the scars that have been left by the Games and&nbsp;
the Capitol's reign of terror linger, Katniss'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:59.440 --> 00:23:04.600
decision to start a family indicates her faith&nbsp;
in the future. Prior to the Games, Katniss swore&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:04.600 --> 00:23:10.200
to never have children, believing she could not&nbsp;
bear to bring them into such a harsh world. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:15.480
despite the horror she has lived through, her only&nbsp;
game is believing the world is worthy of hope.

00:23:15.480 --> 00:23:24.000
"It gets a little tedious after all these&nbsp;
years, but there are much worse games to play."

